  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Point X is at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span> from the centre of Earth. <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span> is larger than the radius of Earth. The gravitational field strength at X is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"g_{x}\"></span>. Point Y is at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3d\"></span> from the centre of Earth.</p>\n<p>What is the difference in the magnitude of gravitational field strengths between X and Y?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{8g_{x}}{9}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3g_{x}}{4}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{g_{x}}{4}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{g_{x}}{9}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
